 "limitations": "The production MythicSim worker shared the machine (load average about 4.6 on 12 cores), so single figures can move by several percent. Go runs as the pinned exporter's sim command, the engine production runs, not the production image's own CLI. Process start is included for both engines, as in production.",
 "findings": [
  "The Rust iteration loop is 1.27 times as fast as Go's (median), and the Rust simulation process peaks at about 7 to 11 MB against about 93 MB for a Go job.",
  "A whole routed job takes about as long as a Go job: median Go over Rust wall time 0.98, 0.98 without the tank builds. The Go exporter's prepare step (median 0.1077 s and about 90 MB), Python and the extra processes use up what the faster loop saves.",
  "Preparing a tank costs far more than simulating it: the exporter exports the target's swing for every stat aura combination, 1.5 s and about 600 MB for the Protection and Fury Protection Warriors and about 0.25 s and 170 MB for the Paladin tanks and the Bear. Routed, those Warrior jobs take 2.8 times as long as in Go.",
  "Four jobs at a time, Go ran 390.3 jobs a minute and routed Rust 315.7, with a peak resident set of 656.3 MB for one routed tank job.",
  "Every routed job gave the same DPS as the pinned Go engine with the same seed."
 ],
